\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] RSTARTVPPROP132
\item[* relevant examples:] x1 envy x3 x2 (Her envied her her house): cf.\ 
Dutch: hij benijdde haar(DONP) om haar huis(PREPNP);
that it is English which is deviant follows from {\em He envied her\/}, which 
has an EMPTY as prepobj in Dutch, which is only possible if the other argument 
is a real dobj, not an indobj. For this deviant ordering, a synIONP\_EMPTY is 
allowed in the pattern rules.
\item[* language:] english
\item[* kind of rule:] M-rule
